# Paths that make a commit "product": changes here alter what a release ships.
# Anything else (docs, site pages, workflows, .claude, Markdown) is non-product.
# README.md is packaged into the release archives but left out on purpose: a
# README-only change doesn't warrant a release.
# One git pathspec per line; a trailing / matches a directory. Read by
# release-prepare.yml, which refuses a release with no product change. Any tool
# that classifies commits the same way should read this file, not copy it.
cmd/
internal/
npm/
plugin/
.claude-plugin/
go.mod
go.sum
Makefile
Dockerfile
LICENSE
site/install.sh
site/install.ps1
